The driver was only configured to support the original version (v1.0) of the IQS7222D device, which does not account for the new revisions (v1.1 and v1.2) that have different memory maps. This oversight would lead to incorrect handling of device operations, causing potential malfunctions.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
.prod_num = IQS7222_PROD_NUM_D,
.fw_major = 1,
.fw_minor = 1,
```
Reason:
By adding support for the new firmware versions (v1.1 and v1.2) with their respective memory maps, the driver can now correctly handle operations for these revisions, ensuring proper functionality and interaction with the hardware.


